        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12429092/comment/12725778",
          "id": "12725778",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=rcmuir&avatarId=10150"
            },
            "displayName": "Robert Muir",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "Simon, I believe fixing the scope issues would reduce the documentation work considerably. For many of the classes that really should not be public, there is still a lot of missing documentation.\n\nIn my opinion, things such as Utility class and everything in .hhmm package should be package-protected. I already wasted time partially javadocing these things, which probably wasn't a complete waste, but you get the idea.\n\nif you look it over, I think you can see I put much more effort into the main analyzer/tokenizer classes that should be public. So these docs are of higher-quality because I think both users and lucene developers will need to interact with these (such as porting to the new Token api, etc).\n\nI think in the short term, I like this patch as is because I think developers will be able to port it to the new API and users will be able to understand what it does.\n\nI can come back around later and do a more thorough job, but this isn't the only analyzer that needs some documentation improvements!\n",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=rcmuir",
            "name": "rcmuir",
            "key": "rcmuir",
            "avatarUrls": {
